  "settings_privacy": "Privacy policy",
  "settings_privacyBody": "Phiotron PDF has no account, no ads, no in-app purchases and no analytics. The developer runs no servers and does not collect your data.\n\nFiles: PDF, Office files and images are processed only on this device and are never uploaded. Files you open or share from other apps are copied into the app's folder; new files are saved on your device and originals are never overwritten. The content search index and settings also stay on the device.\n\nPermissions:\n• Camera: scan documents and take photos.\n• Photos: chosen through the system photo picker; the app only receives the photos you pick.\n• Files: All files access, to find and open documents on this device; files are never uploaded.\n• Fingerprint, face or PIN: for App lock; your device does the check and the app never receives biometric data.\n• Internet: only to download translation language packs from Google when you choose to.\n\nText recognition, QR/barcode reading, document scanning and translation run on the device using Google ML Kit or your system's built-in components. Google ML Kit may send diagnostic and usage data (such as device model, app version and performance metrics, not your files or text) to Google. Read aloud uses your device's text-to-speech engine.\n\nID card photos are only used to create the page you save on this device.\n\nUninstalling the app deletes its data; files you saved to a shared folder remain until you delete them.\n\nContact: phamphuongphuongnd@gmail.com",
